In conclusion, a facile, cost-efficient, environmentally friendly method for $\mathrm{Zr}$ -MOF digestion/regeneration has been developed by utilizing bicarbonate/carbonate solution. As a result, the digested products are all soluble in water, and the regenerated MOF samples have the same structure, specific surface area, and pore structure with their parent MOFs. Well-dispersed Pd nanoparticles were obtained by the digestion process of $\mathrm{Pd}@\mathrm{PCN}-224$ to verify the feasibility of the method. To our knowledge, it is the first case of the complete digestion/ regeneration of $Z\mathrm{r}$ -MOFs. Besides, by analyzing the dynamics of digestion process in bicarbonate and citrate solution, a competition–digestion mechanism actuated by entropy change has been promoted. This facile digestion procedure provides a novel insight for not only ligand recycle, component analysis, nanoparticle synthesis, and drug release but also chemical sensors, extraction–separation, and synthesis materials with unique nanostructure. Although the further optimization and exploration of regeneration process are needed, this novel digestion/regeneration method sheds light on a general MOF digestion and regeneration process and provides access to future applications of MOFs.
## Methods
Synthesis of UiO-66-X ${\bf{\langle}}{\bf{X}}={\bf{\bar{P}}},$ COOH, Br, and NDC). The mixture of BDC (or BDC-COOH, BDC-Br, and NDC), $\mathrm{ZrOCl}_{2}{\bullet}8\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ , benzoic acid, and DMF (mole rati $\mathbf{0}=2{:}1{:}30{:}91\mathrm{\mathrm{.}}$ were sealed in an autoclave. After heating in an isothermal oven at $150^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $48\mathrm{h}$ , the white powder was collected via centrifugalization. The product was washed with DMF and ethanol, and then dried at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under vacuum.
Synthesis of UiO-66-R. In all, $0.200\mathrm{g}$ of UiO-66-P was digested with $5\mathrm{mL}$ of $1\mathbf{M}$ $\mathrm{NH_{4}H C O_{3}}$ aqueous solution. After that, $5\mathrm{mL}$ of 1 M $\scriptstyle1\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{COOH}$ aqueous solution was added into the digestion solution, followed by an evaporation process. Then, the white powdery residue and $3.154\mathrm{g}$ of benzoic acid $25.82\mathrm{mmol}$ ) were dissolved in $6\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF in a vial. Subsequently, the solution was transferred into an autoclave and heated in an isothermal oven at $150^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{48\mathrm{h}}$ . Then, the synthesized UiO-66-R was washed with DMF and ethanol three times, respectively, and finally dried under vacuum at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
Synthesis of PCN-224. In all, $0.06\mathbf{g}$ of $\mathrm{ZrCl_{4}}$ ( $1.73\mathrm{mmol};$ ), $_{0.02\mathrm{g}}$ of TCPP (0.86 mmol), and $0.80\mathrm{g}$ of benzoic acid $\left(25.88\mathrm{mmol}\right.$ ) were dissolved in $4\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF in a pyrex vial and stirred until the solid was dissolved. Then, the solution was heated in an isothermal oven at $120^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $36\mathrm{h}$ . After centrifugalization, the product was washed with DMF and methanol three times, respectively, and finally dried under vacuum at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
Synthesis of PCN-224-R. In all, $0.020\mathrm{g}$ of PCN-224 was digested with $2\mathrm{mL}$ of 1 M $\mathrm{NH_{4}H C O_{3}}$ aqueous solution. After that, $2\mathrm{mL}$ of 1 M $\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{COOH}$ aqueous solution was added into the digestion solution, followed by an evaporation process. Then, the dark-red powdery residue and $0.478{\mathrm{g}}$ of benzoic acid were dissolved in $2.5\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF in a vial. Subsequently, the solution was transferred into an autoclave and heated in an isothermal oven at $120^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $36\mathrm{h}$ . Then, the synthesized PCN-224-R was washed with DMF and ethanol three times, respectively, and finally dried under vacuum at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
Synthesis of Pd@PCN-224. In all, $0.025\mathrm{g}$ of PCN-224 was ultrasonically dispersed in $1\mathrm{mL}$ of ethylene glycol and then preheated at $120^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $10\mathrm{min}$ . After that, $47\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of $0.6\mathbf{M}$ PVP and $23\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of 6 mM ${\mathrm{PdCl}}_{2}$ aqueous solution was added to the ethylene glycol every $30\mathrm{{s}}$ with constant vigorous stirring (total volumes for PVP and ${\mathrm{PdCl}}_{2}$ solutions are 1500 and $750\upmu\mathrm{L}$ , respectively). The resulting mixture was kept at $120^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for an additional $10\mathrm{min}$ and then cooled down to room temperature. The obtained product was washed thoroughly several times with water and ethanol. The synthesized sample was further dried overnight under vacuum at $60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
Digestion experiment. $Z\mathrm{r}$ -MOFs were immersed in $^{1\mathrm{M}}$ salt aqueous solution, after which ultrasonic treatment was performed for $20\mathrm{min}$ .
TCPP recycle. Ten milligrams of PCN-224 was immersed in $3\mathrm{mL}$ of $1\mathbf{M}$ $\mathrm{NH_{4}H C O_{3}}$ aqueous solution, followed by ultrasonic treatment. After complete digestion, 0.1 M HCl was added into the solution drop by drop until no more precipitation was generated. The products were collected by centrifugation and washed with water several times, and finally dried overnight at $80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
XRD measurement. XRD data were recorded on a Rigaku Miniflex600 diffractometer operated at $40\mathrm{kV}$ , $15\mathrm{mA}$ for Cu $\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{a}}$ $\begin{array}{r}{\dot{\langle\lambda=1.5406\tilde{\mathrm{A}}\rangle}}\end{array}$ ) with a scan speed of $5^{\circ}/\mathrm{min}$ and a step size of $0.02^{\circ}$ in $2\theta$ at ambient temperature and pressure.
$\ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}_{2}$ adsorption experiments. $\Nu_{2}$ adsorption experiments were measured on a micromeritics ASAP 2020 HD88 physisorption instrument. A liquid nitrogen bath (77 K) was used for isotherm measurements. High-purity grade $\Nu_{2}$ was used in the adsorption experiments. Before performing the analysis, the sample was outgassed at $150^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ under vacuum for $15\mathrm{h}$ . The multipoint BET analysis was performed by plotting $1/\nu(1-P/P_{0})$ versus $P/P_{0}$ $\mathrm{\Delta}P_{0}=1$ bar) and $\nu$ is the volume of nitrogen adsorbed per gram of MOF at STP. Pore size distributions for MOFs were analyzed by using DFT theory for $\Nu_{2}$ adsorption based on a carbon model.
SEM imaging. SEM measurements were performed on a Zeiss Merlin Compact with an accelerating voltage of $5\mathrm{kV}$ . The samples were placed on clean aluminum foil and sputtered with platinum.
Fourier transform-infrared spectra. All FTIR spectra were recorded on a Nicolet micro FTIR Specrometer iN10 and samples were tableted with KBr powder.
Raman spectra. A Renishaw-RM1000 spectrometer equipped with a CCD detector was used for the Raman studies. A laser with a wavelength of $532\mathrm{nm}$ was applied for excitation. Raman spectra were gathered by using two scans of 10-s exposure each time.
$\pmb{1}_{\pmb{\mathsf{H}}}$ NMR test. All of the $^1\mathrm{H}$ NMR data were collected on Bruker Avance III HD $400\mathrm{MHz}$ nuclear magnetic resonance spectrometer. For digestion, UiO-66 was immersed in $\mathrm{D}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ solution with 1 M $\mathrm{NH_{4}H C O_{3}}$ . Moreover, UiO-66 and BDC were immersed in $\mathrm{D}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ with $\mathrm{NH}_{3}{\bullet}\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ because of the poor solubility of BDC in water. For ligand recycle of PCN-224, the recycled TCPP was immersed in deuterated dimethylsulfoxide.
